35(1)The Lieutenant-Governor in Council may make regulations

(a)
prescribing expenses relating to the administration of the Land Management Fund that are payable out of the Land Management Fund;

(b)
authorizing the Minister to designate lands, buildings and other structures as public works for the purposes of a project, including lands, buildings and other structures referred to in paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition “public work” in section 1;

(c)
authorizing the Minister to revoke a designation made under paragraph (b);

(d)
exempting the lands, buildings and other structures referred to in paragraph (b), or any portion of them, from the application of the Mechanics’ Lien Act, chapter M-6 of the Revised Statutes, 1973.

